{"title": "Show HN: Mobile-friendly image editor inspired by GIMP (layers, selection, etc)", "link": "https://github.com/nielstron/brushkin", "summary": "<p>I don't know if anyone else is still out here crafting memes by hand... but I do! And I find the capabilities of frontier models jarringly bad with this regard. Also... memes are supposed to be made with love!<p>Since I don't always have access to my laptop, I want to be able to do real image editing on my phone. You know.. selection, layering, filters, etc. No OS image editor comes close to this and commercial ones are expensive or cluttered with ads.<p>So I designed a mobile-friendly layout and tasked Claude to port over all of the GIMP tools to this mobile application. It also has some convenience features (AI object selection, tool lookup via BM25), but the core edit loop is similar to GIMP.<p>The filters are the original GIMP filters but almost entirely ported to GPU! So I found it actually very responsive and usable on my potato phone even working on 12MP pictures.<p>I found it fun to play with it and its finally on Google Play now! Let me know what you think :)</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664650\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664650</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-27T09:13:22+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: Mobile-friendly image editor inspired by GIMP (layers, selection, etc)", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://github.com/nielstron/brushkin", "published_at": "2026-11-27T09:13:22+00:00", "summary": "<p>I don't know if anyone else is still out here crafting memes by hand... but I do! And I find the capabilities of frontier models jarringly bad with this regard. Also... memes are supposed to be made with love!<p>Since I don't always have access to my laptop, I want to be able to do real image editing on my phone. You know.. selection, layering, filters, etc. No OS image editor comes close to this and commercial ones are expensive or cluttered with ads.<p>So I designed a mobile-friendly layout and tasked Claude to port over all of the GIMP tools to this mobile application. It also has some convenience features (AI object selection, tool lookup via BM25), but the core edit loop is similar to GIMP.<p>The filters are the original GIMP filters but almost entirely ported to GPU! So I found it actually very responsive and usable on my potato phone even working on 12MP pictures.<p>I found it fun to play with it and its finally on Google Play now! Let me know what you think :)</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664650\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664650</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-11-27T09:28:21.295173+00:00"}
{"title": "Feels like AI model dumbed down purposefully", "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664618", "summary": "<p>My codex is still running on sol5.6. Did not upgrade the model yet. But have noticed the model has become dumb this week compared to last week. Feels like this is purposefully. Anyone else?</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664618\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664618</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-27T09:08:23+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Feels like AI model dumbed down purposefully", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664618", "published_at": "2026-11-27T09:08:23+00:00", "summary": "<p>My codex is still running on sol5.6. Did not upgrade the model yet. But have noticed the model has become dumb this week compared to last week. Feels like this is purposefully. Anyone else?</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664618\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50664618</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-11-27T09:28:21.295173+00:00"}
